@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1352 = private unnamed_addr constant [28 x i8] c"docstring-extraneous-returns", align 1
@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1353 = private unnamed_addr constant [836 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for function docstrings with unnecessary \22Returns\22 sections.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AA function without an explicit `return` statement should not have a\0A\22Returns\22 section in its docstring.\0A\0AThis rule is not enforced for abstract methods. It is also ignored for\0A\22stub functions\22: functions where the body only consists of `pass`, `...`,\0A`raise NotImplementedError`, or similar.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef say_hello(n: int) -> None:\0A    \22\22\22Says hello to the user.\0A\0A    Args:\0A        n: Number of times to say hello.\0A\0A    Returns:\0A        Doesn't return anything.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    for _ in range(n):\0A        print(\22Hello!\22)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef say_hello(n: int) -> None:\0A    \22\22\22Says hello to the user.\0A\0A    Args:\0A        n: Number of times to say hello.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    for _ in range(n):\0A        print(\22Hello!\22)\0A```\0A", align 1
