@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1364 = private unnamed_addr constant [27 x i8] c"docstring-missing-exception", align 1
@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1365 = private unnamed_addr constant [1431 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for function docstrings that do not document all explicitly raised\0Aexceptions.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AA function should document all exceptions that are directly raised in some\0Acircumstances. Failing to document an exception that could be raised\0Acan be misleading to users and/or a sign of incomplete documentation.\0A\0AThis rule is not enforced for abstract methods. It is also ignored for\0A\22stub functions\22: functions where the body only consists of `pass`, `...`,\0A`raise NotImplementedError`, or similar.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef calculate_speed(distance: float, time: float) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Calculate speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Args:\0A        distance: Distance traveled.\0A        time: Time spent traveling.\0A\0A    Returns:\0A        Speed as distance divided by time.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    try:\0A        return distance / time\0A    except ZeroDivisionError as exc:\0A        raise FasterThanLightError from exc\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef calculate_speed(distance: float, time: float) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Calculate speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Args:\0A        distance: Distance traveled.\0A        time: Time spent traveling.\0A\0A    Returns:\0A        Speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Raises:\0A        FasterThanLightError: If speed is greater than the speed of light.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    try:\0A        return distance / time\0A    except ZeroDivisionError as exc:\0A        raise FasterThanLightError from exc\0A```\0A", align 1
