@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1381 = private unnamed_addr constant [1047 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for docstrings in which the first line does not end in a period.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A[PEP 257] recommends that the first line of a docstring is written in the\0Aform of a command, ending in a period.\0A\0AThis rule may not apply to all projects; its applicability is a matter of\0Aconvention. By default, this rule is enabled when using the `numpy` and\0A`pep257` conventions, and disabled when using the `google` convention.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef average(values: list[float]) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Return the mean of the given values\22\22\22\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef average(values: list[float]) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Return the mean of the given values.\22\22\22\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pydocstyle.convention`\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A- [Google Python Style Guide - Docstrings](https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#38-comments-and-docstrings)\0A\0A[PEP 257]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/\0A", align 1
