@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1410 = private unnamed_addr constant [1902 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for section headers in docstrings that do not begin with capital\0Aletters.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AFor stylistic consistency, all section headers in a docstring should be\0Acapitalized.\0A\0AMultiline docstrings are typically composed of a summary line, followed by\0Aa blank line, followed by a series of sections. Each section typically has\0Aa header and a body.\0A\0AThis rule is enabled when using the `numpy` and `google` conventions, and\0Adisabled when using the `pep257` convention.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef calculate_speed(distance: float, time: float) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Calculate speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    args:\0A        distance: Distance traveled.\0A        time: Time spent traveling.\0A\0A    returns:\0A        Speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    raises:\0A        FasterThanLightError: If speed is greater than the speed of light.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    try:\0A        return distance / time\0A    except ZeroDivisionError as exc:\0A        raise FasterThanLightError from exc\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef calculate_speed(distance: float, time: float) -> float:\0A    \22\22\22Calculate speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Args:\0A        distance: Distance traveled.\0A        time: Time spent traveling.\0A\0A    Returns:\0A        Speed as distance divided by time.\0A\0A    Raises:\0A        FasterThanLightError: If speed is greater than the speed of light.\0A    \22\22\22\0A    try:\0A        return distance / time\0A    except ZeroDivisionError as exc:\0A        raise FasterThanLightError from exc\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.pydocstyle.convention`\0A\0A## References\0A- [PEP 257 \E2\80\93 Docstring Conventions](https://peps.python.org/pep-0257/)\0A- [PEP 287 \E2\80\93 reStructuredText Docstring Format](https://peps.python.org/pep-0287/)\0A- [NumPy Style Guide](https://numpydoc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/format.html)\0A- [Google Python Style Guide - Docstrings](https://google.github.io/styleguide/pyguide.html#38-comments-and-docstrings)\0A", align 1
