@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1488 = private unnamed_addr constant [1049 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `except` blocks that handle all exceptions, but are not the last\0A`except` block in a `try` statement.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen an exception is raised within a `try` block, the `except` blocks are\0Aevaluated in order, and the first matching block is executed. If an `except`\0Ablock handles all exceptions, but isn't the last block, Python will raise a\0A`SyntaxError`, as the following blocks would never be executed.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef reciprocal(n):\0A    try:\0A        reciprocal = 1 / n\0A    except:\0A        print(\22An exception occurred.\22)\0A    except ZeroDivisionError:\0A        print(\22Cannot divide by zero.\22)\0A    else:\0A        return reciprocal\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef reciprocal(n):\0A    try:\0A        reciprocal = 1 / n\0A    except ZeroDivisionError:\0A        print(\22Cannot divide by zero.\22)\0A    except:\0A        print(\22An exception occurred.\22)\0A    else:\0A        return reciprocal\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `except` clause](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/compound_stmts.html#except-clause)\0A", align 1
