@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1548 = private unnamed_addr constant [499 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `datetime.timezone.utc`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAs of Python 3.11, `datetime.UTC` is an alias for `datetime.timezone.utc`.\0AThe alias is more readable and generally preferred over the full path.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport datetime\0A\0Adatetime.timezone.utc\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport datetime\0A\0Adatetime.UTC\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `target-version`\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `datetime.UTC`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/datetime.html#datetime.UTC)\0A", align 1
