@anon.8cc3e55251025b29006123e4bed3261b.1596 = private unnamed_addr constant [731 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `typing.NoReturn` and `typing.Never` in union types.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0A`typing.NoReturn` and `typing.Never` are special types, used to indicate\0Athat a function never returns, or that a type has no values.\0A\0AIncluding `typing.NoReturn` or `typing.Never` in a union type is redundant,\0Aas, e.g., `typing.Never | T` is equivalent to `T`.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Afrom typing import Never\0A\0A\0Adef func() -> Never | int: ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Adef func() -> int: ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `typing.Never`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Never)\0A- [Python documentation: `typing.NoReturn`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.NoReturn)\0A", align 1
